From faf8e1e2715b9e0818de0bcb4b8356fe53c02727 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:42:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(copy-drafts): prefer useful continuations among equal
 suffix matches

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus the candidate-38 series (head 1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4).

A latest-position tie break can offer just one token on repetitive text although an equally strong earlier match has a full continuation. Rank equal-length matches by available continuation capped at the lookahead, then recency. Encode this as an int32 priority for deterministic max reductions. Decode it consistently in allocation and selection, and include lookahead in warmup keys. Retain shorter copies when no full continuation exists. Include allocation in the bundled pipeline benchmark.

Quality: draft selection changes; target verification and acceptance arithmetic do not. No cross-request state or host synchronization is added. End-to-end speedup requires serving qualification.

Tests: independent NumPy references, full/short boundary cases across scan passes and lookaheads, allocation agreement through cap growth, CUDA replay, request reuse and committed-text invariance. GPU receipts are retained in the deployment experiment.

Upstream status: local candidate, not submitted.
